  "limits": [
    "Route-set evidence only: the oracle is the framework route table read at import time. Nothing in this record issued an HTTP request, so no entry is Runtime-tested.",
    "HEAD and OPTIONS are dropped on both sides. A scanner pair whose method is null compares as \"-\" and is reported as unresolved when the oracle has a real method for that path, never as an exact match.",
    "An outcome of flagged means the named flag is present in the layer output for that fixture and the covers text says why it applies; it is not proof the layer understood the construct. A flag that also fires on exact fixtures is not counted as covering unless the missed construct is the one it names.",
    "CI does not reinstall the framework: the stored oracle output is bound by sha256, by the pin and by the sha256 of oracle.py. Only the in-repo static scanners are re-run live, which needs python3 on PATH (a missing python3 fails the verification, it is never skipped).",
    "Only the pinned version was run. Releases uploaded after the pinned wheel are listed per package and are not covered.",
    "record_digest seals the whole record, so an edit that is not re-sealed fails. Prose is sealed, not recomputed: statement, reasons, limits, plan, oracle_range text, layer roles, construct and covers texts are not derived from evidence, so a re-sealed prose edit is not detected by the verifier and must be caught in review.",
    "The T06 registration-limitation flag also fires on exact fixtures that register a Blueprint; it is counted as covering only for the url_prefix override fixture, where its text names url_prefix.",
    "The pallets/flask examples/tutorial ref in FLASK_PROFILE.versionPin is a historical real-repo comparison pin whose framework version is null in the profile; it is not what was run here and no claim is made for it."
  ],
